    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nAfter https://github.com/neovim/neovim/commit/29a46a11aa0820e4efcad80a2dfb9ca600924f58 Neovim with ui2 enabled shows empty row in place of the statusline after saving the buffer (`:w`). Statusline is redrawn correctly after moving cursor, etc.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n```\nnvim --clean <some file>\n:lua require(\"vim._core.ui2\").enable({})\n:set cmdheight=0\n:w\n```\n### Expected behavior\n\nBehave just like before aforementioned commit: do not draw an empty row over statusline.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-6234+g8adf6e769f-Homebrew\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno ui2 in vim\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS 15.7\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwezterm 20260823-230148-f93d9035\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nwezterm\n\n### Installation\n\nHomebrew",
